---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Nature of the derived work
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The port from Go to MoonBit is a re-implementation, not a line-by-line
translation, so it is not a byte-for-byte copy of the upstream source.
However, this is explicitly NOT a clean-room implementation. The following
are carried over from the upstream Go SDK and are the parts of this work
that Apache-2.0 actually covers:

  - public API names (e.g. `CreateCollection`, `NewSearchOption`)
  - struct/field names (e.g. `FieldSchema`, `CollectionSchema`)
  - protocol constant values (e.g. `FieldType = 101`, `DataType` numbers)
  - option constructor names and option semantics
  - default values and metric/index type literals

Per-file provenance for ported source files is recorded in the header
comment of each file, in the form:

  // 移植自 github.com/milvus-io/milvus client/<path> (Apache-2.0)
  // Copyright (c) LF AI & Data Foundation

Upstream itself ships no NOTICE file at its repository root, so there is no
upstream NOTICE to inherit. This NOTICE is created on our own initiative to
record provenance and the scope of the derived work.

